# This Mac

This Mac's setup (command-line tools, apps, dotfiles, macOS settings and
Claude Code's own settings) is managed by chezmoi from the cradle repo, at
`chezmoi source-path` (normally `~/Documents/cradle`).

When asked to install, update, change or remove anything about this machine's
setup, from any folder, read that repo's CLAUDE.md and make the change there.
Don't edit the managed files in `~` directly, and don't install tools
globally with `brew install`, `npm install -g`, `pip install`, `uv tool
install` or `go install`; they belong in the repo's mise config or Brewfile.
Project dependencies inside a project are fine.

# Memory (agentdb)

The `agentdb` MCP server is a memory of past work that lasts between
sessions. It already keeps work and personal apart by the folder Claude
started in, so never pick or mention a database.

- Before starting a task that takes real work (a bug, a feature, a change
  across files, an investigation), call `reflexion_retrieve` with a one-line
  description of the task. Use what's relevant; ignore what isn't.
- When such a task ends, whether it worked or not, call `reflexion_store`:
  `session_id` as `<folder name>-<YYYY-MM-DD>`, `task` in one line, `success`,
  `reward` from 0 to 1, and a `critique` of a few sentences: what worked, what
  didn't, what to do differently next time.
- Store only lessons. Never store secrets, tokens, credentials, personal
  details, or anything from folders Claude must not read.
- Skip both for quick questions, lookups and one-line edits, and in
  scheduled headless runs such as the journal. If agentdb isn't connected,
  carry on without it.
