# Obsidian

{{- if and .workVault .personalVault }}

The user has two Obsidian vaults, plain Markdown files (each backed up
nightly to a private git repo by `vault-sync`, when one is set):

- Work: `{{ .workVault }}`, structured, with daily notes and the journal.
- Personal: `{{ .personalVault }}`, unstructured and ad hoc.

Use the vault that matches the session: the work vault when the folder the
session started in is work (`is-work <folder>` exits 0; check once, when a
vault is first needed), otherwise the personal one. Reach into the other
vault only when the user asks.
{{- else if .workVault }}

The user's work Obsidian vault is `{{ .workVault }}`: plain Markdown files,
structured, with daily notes and the journal.
{{- else }}

The user's personal Obsidian vault is `{{ .personalVault }}`: plain Markdown
files, unstructured and ad hoc.
{{- end }}

Read, search and link notes in it whenever it helps, from any project.
{{- $private := list }}
{{- range list (list .workVault .workVaultPrivate) (list .personalVault .personalVaultPrivate) }}
{{-   $vault := index . 0 }}
{{-   if $vault }}
{{-     range splitList ";" (index . 1) }}{{ $f := trim . | trimSuffix "/" }}{{ if $f }}{{ $private = append $private (printf "%s/%s" $vault $f) }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{-   end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if $private }}

Never read these folders, with file tools, `grep`, `cat` or any other
command. Claude Code's permissions block its file tools there; shell commands
are kept out only by this rule.
{{- range $private }}
- `{{ . }}`
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

- Write the Obsidian way: `[[wikilinks]]` to other notes, properties (YAML
  frontmatter) where notes use them, attachments where the vault keeps them.
- Add or edit notes when asked, or when a skill says to. Never move, rename or
  delete notes, or change `.obsidian/`, without asking.
{{- if .workVault }}
- In the work vault, the Daily notes and Templates settings and its
  templates are managed from the cradle repo's `obsidian/` folder; change
  them there, not in the vault.
- The `journal` skill writes the day's work Claude Code sessions and git
  commits into the work vault's daily note; a LaunchAgent runs it every
  evening at 18:00.
{{- end }}
{{- if .personalVault }}
- The personal vault has no set structure: no daily notes or templates from
  cradle. Follow whatever the user's notes there already do, and keep work
  content out of it. Its `cradle.md` note holds private notes about the
  cradle setup (hosts, orgs, quirks) that every machine needs but the public
  repo can't hold; read it when working on cradle, and add to it there.
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
